  "scope": "Conservation bound, no QA independence assumption. Every shipped pump consumes one distinct housing, rotor and flange blank; replacements consume extra stock. Only the held scheduled material delivery can add blanks; paid capacity option adds a calibration tool. Timing, quality and all resource conflicts are optimistically free. Passing this bound proves no feasible schedule.",
  "conclusion": "32 initial orders is the largest integer count whose material-only bound permits all orders on every rush/no-rush branch. At33 or34 initial, all-fulfilled probability is at most0.5; at35 ormore it is zero. This does not prove any tested policy attains those ceilings.",
